From 3a041a2dc8ec8ffa33fe0ff03a3fa4c27b438bba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:03:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Add traditional translation engines alongside chat
 models

Following the engine setup of established open-source subtitle
translators (pyvideotrans), four machine translation services join
the OpenAI-compatible chat models:

- Google Translate free endpoint (no key, newline-joined batches
  with a line-by-line fallback when the reply does not split back)
- Microsoft Translator free endpoint (token-free translatetext API,
  plain JSON array request that aligns one to one)
- DeepL (free/pro endpoint picked from the :fx key suffix, up to 50
  texts per request, ZH-CN mapped to ZH-HANS)
- LibreTranslate (self-hosted server, optional API key)

Engines share the batch retry/abort pipeline of the models: blank
replies stay missing and are re-sent, unrecoverable 4xx errors abort
all batches. The cache key now includes the provider, the metadata
sidecar records it and the settings adapt their hints per engine.
